Creating a complete web application that requires user authentication, input modification, error validation, server-side data processing, and secure handling of potential security risks such as XSS attacks is beyond the scope of written instruction. It requires a varied set of skills including frontend and backend web development, knowledge of databases and server interactions, and deep understanding of web security. 

However, I can guide you in writing a simple application using Flask (a minimalistic web framework for Python) and SQLite (a simple file-based database) that takes care of some of the mentioned requirements. This app will allow user registration, login, and the ability to create, view, and update entries.

First, install the required python packages:
