To merge two sorted arrays into a single sorted array, you can use the merge sort algorithm. The merge sort algorithm works by dividing the array into smaller subarrays, sorting them recursively, and then merging them back together. Here's a Java implementation:

```java
public class MergeSortedArrays {

    public static void merge(int[] arr1, int[] arr2, int[] result) {
        int i = 0, j = 0, k = 0;

        while (i < arr1.length && j < arr2.length) {
            if (arr1[i] < arr2[j]) {
                result[k++] = arr1[i++];
            } else {
                result[k++] = arr2[j++];
            }
        }

        while (i < arr1.length) {
            result[k++] = arr1[i++];
        }

        while (j < arr2.length) {
            result[k++] = arr2[j++];
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] arr1 = { 1, 3, 5, 7 };
        int[] arr2 = { 2, 4, 6, 8 };
        int[] result = new int[arr1.length + arr2.length];

        merge(arr1, arr2, result);

        System.out.print("Merged array: ");
        for (int num : result) {
            System.out.print(num + " ");
        }
    }
}
```

Output:
```
Merged array: 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8
```

In this implementation, we use three pointers `i`, `j`, and `k` to keep track of the indices in `arr1`, `arr2`, and `result` respectively. We compare the elements at these indices and add the smaller element to the `result` array. We increment the corresponding indices and continue this process until we reach the end of either `arr1` or `arr2`. Finally, we copy any remaining elements from `arr1` or `arr2` to `result`.

