     *
     * @param string $licenseKey The license key to retrieve the license for.
     * @return License The retrieved License object.
     */
    public function getLicense(string $licenseKey): License
    {
        $httpClient = new Client();
        $response = $httpClient->get('https://api.keygen.sh/v1/licenses/' . $licenseKey);
        $licenseData = json_decode($response->getBody(), true);

        $license = new License();
        $license->setId($licenseData['id']);
        $license->setKey($licenseData['key']);
        $license->setValid($licenseData['valid']);
        $license->setExpiresAt(new \DateTime($licenseData['expiresAt']));
        $license->setMetadata($licenseData['metadata']);

        return $license;
    }
}
```
In the solution, we use the Guzzle HTTP client to make a GET request to the Keygen.sh API endpoint with the provided `$licenseKey`. We then parse the JSON response and use the retrieved data to construct a `License` object. The `License` object is populated with the relevant information from the API response and returned as the result of the `getLicense` method.

